# pyenv
#   For a library or package, you might want to ignore these files since the code is
#   temporary; see:
#   https://docs.python.org/3.10/tutorial/modules.html#compiled-source-files
.python-version

# pipenv
#   According to pypa/pipenv#598, it is recommended to include Pipfile.lock in version control.
#   However, in case of collaboration, if having platform-specific dependencies or having
#   no platform-specific dependencies, the contributors may have different generated files.
#Pipfile.lock

# poetry
#   Similar to Pipfile.lock, it is generally recommended to include poetry.lock in version control.
#   This is especially recommended for binary packages to ensure reproducibility, and is more
#   commonly ignored for libraries.
#   https://python-poetry.org/docs/basic-usage/#committing-your-poetry-lock-file-to-version-control
#poetry.lock

